# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Zola build output. `/public/` too: `--output-dir` resolves against the working
# directory rather than `--root`, so a stray invocation lands it at the repo root.
site/public/
/public/

# Primary sources (see specs/README.md). Third-party publications — BNetzA
# Festlegungen, BDEW/VKU/GEODE Leitfäden, EDI@Energy Codelisten, VDE FNN
# Hinweise — redistributed under their own terms, so they are staged rather
# than committed. `just specs` rebuilds the folder from the index.
/specs/

# Internal design notes (see concepts/README.md). Working documents: they quote
# the regulatory sources by clause and page, and record what each design
# decision cost. `site/` is the public narrative, `CHANGELOG.md` the history and
# the rustdoc the API contract; `concepts/` is none of the three, and nothing in
# the build reads it.
/concepts/
